## Failure modes

| What can go wrong | How mtix behaves | What you do |
|---|---|---|
| `.mtix/data/mtix.db` corrupted | Read/write fails with a clear error | Restore from `.mtix/tasks.json` via `mtix import`; commit a fresh snapshot |
| Two agents on same machine race a write | SQLite WAL + busy_timeout serialize writes | No action; this is the supported concurrent topology for solo mode |
| **Hub unreachable** | N/A — solo mode does not use a sync hub | Switch to small-team workflow before adding remote collaborators |
| **Hook bypassed** (`git push --no-verify`) | tasks.json may lag the DB | Re-export with `mtix export` and commit |
| **Schema mismatch** after upgrade | Startup migration runs automatically; failure aborts | `mtix verify`, then re-run; report a bug if migration loops |
| **Queue full** | N/A — sync queue is empty in solo mode | Not applicable to solo mode |
| **Lost laptop** | The git-tracked `.mtix/tasks.json` is your only off-machine copy | Restore from a fresh clone via `mtix import` — see "Disaster recovery" below |
| **Divergent history** | N/A — solo mode has only one source of events | Not applicable to solo mode |
| **Auto-import refused** after a `git pull` or checkout (`mtix: auto-import of .mtix/tasks.json refused`) | The pulled `.mtix/tasks.json` lacks tasks, comments, activity, dependencies or field values this store holds (a stale snapshot, or one from mtix older than 0.5.4). Nothing is imported; the refusal repeats on every command, and writes stay in the store without rewriting the snapshot | Read the list, then run `mtix import .mtix/tasks.json --mode merge` (keeps every local node and dependency, every comment, activity entry and value the refusal lists, and decides the other field values per task: when the task's content (title, description, prompt, acceptance, labels) matches the file's, yours win, and otherwise the file's copy wins, undoing your edits to that task; afterwards check `git log -p .mtix/tasks.json` and reapply what it undid; a task listed as `a different task under this id` is renumbered to the next free number, applied only with `--confirm`), `mtix sync --fix` (keeps the store, rewrites the file) or `mtix import .mtix/tasks.json --mode replace` (the file wins). `mtix sync` shows the refusal. For a conflict although you changed nothing locally (after an upgrade), see [A conflict although nothing changed locally](../TROUBLESHOOTING.md#a-conflict-although-nothing-changed-locally) |

